              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "当心 (dāngxīn) is built from 当 and 心 'the heart', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tang and sim (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to match' and 'to preside'. How the pair came to mean watching out is not settled."
